make-affidavits API Reference

A comprehensive API specification for creating, managing, and validating affidavit drafts.

Overview

The make-affidavits API is designed to help applications create structured affidavit drafts, validate required information, retrieve existing drafts, and manage supporting exhibit details.

Base URL: https://api.example.com/v1

Content-Type: application/json

Authentication

Authentication requirements depend on the implementation. If authentication is enabled, include the required credentials in the request headers.

Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

Endpoints

|Method|Endpoint              |Description                   |
|------|----------------------|------------------------------|
|POST  |`/affidavits`         |Create an affidavit draft     |
|GET   |`/affidavits/{id}`    |Retrieve an affidavit draft   |
|PUT   |`/affidavits/{id}`    |Update an affidavit draft     |
|DELETE|`/affidavits/{id}`    |Delete an affidavit draft     |
|POST  |`/affidavits/validate`|Validate affidavit information|

These endpoints describe the proposed API and must be implemented before they can be used.

────────

1. Create an Affidavit

Creates an affidavit draft using the supplied court details, deponent information, facts, and optional exhibits.

Endpoint: POST /affidavits

Request body

{
  "court": {
    "name": "High Court of Lagos State",
    "division": "Ikeja Judicial Division",
    "location": "Ikeja",
    "suitNumber": "LD/123/2026"
  },
  "parties": {
    "claimant": "Jane Doe",
    "defendant": "John Smith"
  },
  "purpose": "Proof of residence",
  "deponent": {
    "fullName": "Jane Doe",
    "occupation": "Teacher",
    "nationality": "Nigerian",
    "address": "Lagos, Nigeria",
    "capacity": "Claimant"
  },
  "facts": [
    "I am the claimant in this matter.",
    "I reside at the address stated above."
  ],
  "exhibits": [
    {
      "mark": "A",
      "description": "Proof of residence document"
    }
  ],
  "jurat": {
    "location": "Ikeja",
    "date": "2026-10-17"
  }
}

Successful response

Status: 201 Created

{
  "id": "aff-001",
  "status": "draft",
  "message": "Affidavit draft created successfully."
}

────────

2. Retrieve an Affidavit

Retrieves a previously created affidavit draft by its unique identifier.

Endpoint: GET /affidavits/{id}

Path parameters

|Parameter|Type  |Required|Description                |
|---------|------|--------|---------------------------|
|`id`     |string|Yes     |Unique affidavit identifier|

Example request

GET /affidavits/aff-001

Successful response

Status: 200 OK

{
  "id": "aff-001",
  "purpose": "Proof of residence",
  "status": "draft",
  "deponent": {
    "fullName": "Jane Doe",
    "occupation": "Teacher",
    "nationality": "Nigerian",
    "address": "Lagos, Nigeria",
    "capacity": "Claimant"
  },
  "facts": [
    "I am the claimant in this matter.",
    "I reside at the address stated above."
  ]
}

────────

3. Update an Affidavit

Updates an existing affidavit draft.

Endpoint: PUT /affidavits/{id}

Path parameters

|Parameter|Type  |Required|Description                |
|---------|------|--------|---------------------------|
|`id`     |string|Yes     |Unique affidavit identifier|

Request body

Supply the updated affidavit data according to the schema used by the API.

{
  "purpose": "Confirmation of residence",
  "facts": [
    "I am the claimant in this matter.",
    "I currently reside at the address stated in this affidavit."
  ]
}

Successful response

Status: 200 OK

{
  "id": "aff-001",
  "status": "updated",
  "message": "Affidavit draft updated successfully."
}

────────

4. Delete an Affidavit

Deletes an existing affidavit draft.

Endpoint: DELETE /affidavits/{id}

Path parameters

|Parameter|Type  |Required|Description                |
|---------|------|--------|---------------------------|
|`id`     |string|Yes     |Unique affidavit identifier|

Successful response

Status: 204 No Content

No response body is returned.

────────

5. Validate Affidavit Information

Checks whether the supplied information contains the required fields for an affidavit draft.

Endpoint: POST /affidavits/validate

Request body

{
  "deponent": {
    "fullName": "Jane Doe",
    "occupation": "Teacher",
    "nationality": "Nigerian",
    "address": "Lagos, Nigeria",
    "capacity": "Claimant"
  },
  "purpose": "Proof of residence",
  "facts": [
    "I reside at the address stated in this affidavit."
  ]
}

Successful response

Status: 200 OK

{
  "valid": true,
  "errors": []
}

Validation failure response

{
  "valid": false,
  "errors": [
    {
      "field": "deponent.fullName",
      "message": "Full name is required."
    }
  ]
}

The validation rules must be defined by the implementation and adapted to the applicable court requirements.

────────

Data Models

Deponent

|Field        |Type  |Required|
|-------------|------|--------|
|`fullName`   |string|Yes     |
|`occupation` |string|Yes     |
|`nationality`|string|Yes     |
|`address`    |string|Yes     |
|`capacity`   |string|Yes     |

Court

|Field       |Type  |Required     |
|------------|------|-------------|
|`name`      |string|Yes          |
|`division`  |string|As applicable|
|`location`  |string|Yes          |
|`suitNumber`|string|As applicable|

Fact

Each fact is represented as a string in an ordered array. Facts should be relevant, clear, concise, and appropriately based on the deponent’s knowledge.

Exhibit

|Field        |Type  |Required                        |
|-------------|------|--------------------------------|
|`mark`       |string|Yes, when an exhibit is included|
|`description`|string|Yes                             |

The exhibit metadata describes supporting documents. Actual document uploads require additional implementation.

Jurat

|Field     |Type  |Required                                     |
|----------|------|---------------------------------------------|
|`location`|string|Yes                                          |
|`date`    |string|Yes; use `YYYY-MM-DD` in this proposed schema|

The jurat must be adapted to the applicable legal and procedural requirements.

